222
00:15:31,474 --> 00:15:32,334
the same file.

223
00:15:36,174 --> 00:15:40,161
Answer out loud. The question asks for
an order and a reason per command.

224
00:15:40,201 --> 00:15:44,739
A strong answer starts with the command
whose first line can change everything that

225
00:15:44,779 --> 00:15:49,317
follows, moves from the current state to
the history of the refs to the server, and

226
00:15:49,357 --> 00:15:51,854
says for each command
what it rules in or out.

227
00:15:52,194 --> 00:15:56,821
It distinguishes the reflog of a branch
from the reflog of HEAD and says when only

228
00:15:56,861 --> 00:16:01,260
one of them exists. It includes the
command for work that was staged and never

229
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:05,927
