files. It ends with the first change you

230
00:16:05,967 --> 00:16:08,887
would make, and why that
change can't lose anything.

231
00:16:10,727 --> 00:16:11,654
Let's land this.

232
00:16:11,994 --> 00:16:16,945
After a hard reset, committed work is in
the reflog, staged work is in dangling

233
00:16:16,985 --> 00:16:19,915
blobs without names, and
unstaged work is gone.

234
00:16:20,255 --> 00:16:24,678
Recover by adding the lost commits on top
of the current tip, not by moving the

235
00:16:24,718 --> 00:16:25,356
branch back.

236
00:16:25,696 --> 00:16:30,909
A branch's reflog is deleted with the branch;
the reflog of HEAD survives and holds

237
00:16:30,949 --> 00:16:31,416
the tip.

238
00:16:31,756 --> 00:16:36,401
After a squash merge, compare trees, not
patch IDs, to find which work is where.

239
00:16:36,741 --> 00:16:41,479
Tell the person exactly what is back, what
is not and why, and which command was not

240
00:16:41,519 --> 00:16:41,991
involved.

241
00:16:43,831 --> 00:16:48,242
Read sections 30.5 and 30.12.
Compare your own attempt with

242
